  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91036662a85844eb162bdfbe2ea8ce9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: AmericanRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  displayName: American
  description: Standard 8x8 checkers - men capture only forward, any legal capture is playable.
  longDescription: "<b>Basic Movement</b>\nDark Squares Only: pieces always stay on the dark squares. Forward Only: regular pieces (men) can only move diagonally forward. One Square: standard moves are exactly one square into an adjacent empty space.\n\n<b>Capture Mechanics</b>\nThe Jump: capture an opponent's piece by jumping diagonally over it into an empty square directly behind it. Mandatory Jumps: if a jump is available on your turn, you must take it. Multi-Jumps: if your piece lands and has another legal jump available, you must continue jumping in the same turn. Removal: captured pieces are immediately taken off the board.\n\n<b>Kinging (Crowning)</b>\nReaching the End: when a piece reaches the farthest row, it becomes a King. Two-Way Movement: Kings can move and capture both forward and backward diagonally. Turn Resolution: if a piece becomes a King during a jumping sequence, its turn ends immediately - it can't use its new backward powers until the next turn.\n\n<b>Winning the Game</b>\nElimination: capturing all of your opponent's pieces. Blockade: trapping your opponent so they have no legal moves left on their turn."
  rows: 8
  columns: 8
  pieceRowsPerSide: 3
  movementScheme: 0
  piecesOnAllSquares: 0
  leaveBackRowEmpty: 0
  flyingKings: 0
  menCaptureBackward: 0
  menCannotCaptureKings: 0
  mustCaptureMaximum: 0
  preferKingMover: 0
  preferKingCaptures: 0
  preferEarlierKingCapture: 0
  midChainPromotionRule: 1
  deferCaptureRemoval: 0
  forbidImmediateReversal: 0
  noProgressMoveLimit: 40
  singleManLosesToKing: 0
